{
 "section_summary": "Pages 31–40 finish an earlier issue of Radio Tokyo with articles on Japanese nursing, army life, parks, history, language, education, and overseas broadcasting. Pages 41–48 contain January 1941 material, including arguments for Japan’s leadership in East Asia, cultural essays, programme listings, and French and Dutch notices to listeners. Pages 49–53 begin the February 1941 issue with a cover, broadcast schedule, political essay, and art feature.",
